ReplayKit patch 1 of 4 for win-capture-audio 2.3.4 (Ayrton09, commit d11b381).

Exclude mode keeps following the audio sessions of every other program, as the 2.2.x plugin did, and never switches to
the native single client that captures everything except one process tree. ReplayKit
depends on the older behaviour for the desktop audio source: its exclude list names the obs processes (obs64, the cef
pages, the helper) so their sound is never captured, and the single client cannot leave out more than one tree. With
one excluded program playing (Discord in a call) the single client would capture the monitoring output of obs itself
again, and the capture would also restart every time an excluded program starts or stops playing.

